extends /views/templates/layouts/_base

append variables
	- pagetitle = "Features | Legends"
	- pagedescription = "Legends in Tablechart: the names of lines or slices, in a row under the chart."

block content
	.lane
		.container
			.page-header
				h1 Legends
				p.lead The names of the lines or slices, in a row under the chart.

	+section("Legend for several lines")
		p On a line chart with several lines, the names are shown at the end of the lines. Add #[code data-chart-legend] to the figure to show them in a legend under the chart instead. Each name has a short sample of its line.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="line" data-chart-legend)
				figcaption: b Apples per tree
				table
					thead
						tr
							th Year
							th North
							th South
							th East
					tbody
						each row in [['2016', '41', '30', '22'], ['2019', '58', '39', '35'], ['2022', '77', '52', '41'], ['2025', '105', '61', '70']]
							tr
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]
								td= row[2]
								td= row[3]

		p To use a legend for every chart, set the #[code legend] option. Then #[code data-chart-legend="false"] turns it off for one chart.

		+codeblock('JS').
			init({ legend: true });

	+section("Area, column and bar legends")
		p In an area chart, #[code data-chart-legend] works the same way. Each name has a square of the colour of its area.
		p A grouped or stacked column or bar chart always has a legend under the chart, with a square for each name.

	+section("Donut legend")
		p A donut chart always has a legend under the ring. See #[a(href=url('/types/donut.html')) Donut].

	+section("Style the legend")
		p A legend is as wide as its items. These variables set its background, border, padding and corners. By default, there are none.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="line" data-chart-legend style="--tablechart-legend-border: 1px solid currentColor; --tablechart-legend-padding: 0.3em 0.8em; --tablechart-legend-radius: 0.4em")
				table
					thead
						tr
							th Year
							th North
							th South
					tbody
						each row in [['2016', '41', '30'], ['2019', '58', '39'], ['2022', '77', '52'], ['2025', '105', '61']]
							tr
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]
								td= row[2]

		table
			thead
				tr
					th Variable
					th Sets
			tbody
				tr
					td: code --tablechart-legend-surface
					td The background
				tr
					td: code --tablechart-legend-border
					td The border
				tr
					td: code --tablechart-legend-padding
					td The space inside the border
				tr
					td: code --tablechart-legend-radius
					td The corners
				tr
					td: code --tablechart-legend-gap
					td The space above the legend of a line chart
